menu "Bedside clock"

    config BEDSIDE_WAKE_MWW
        bool "Wake word: microWakeWord streaming model (tflite-micro) instead of WakeNet"
        default n
        help
            Detect the wake word with the embedded microWakeWord model
            (main/models/wake_word.tflite + .json manifest) running on
            esp-tflite-micro with ESP-NN PIE kernels, fed from the esp-sr AFE
            output. WakeNet is then not initialised (saves ~324 KB PSRAM and
            ~14 % of a core); MultiNet, VAD and the LocalAI stages are
            unchanged. Off = the stock esp-sr WakeNet9 "Hi ESP".
            Build the variant with:
              idf.py -B build_mww -D SDKCONFIG=sdkconfig.mww \
                -D "SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS=sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.mww.defaults" build

endmenu
